[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4757914152","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120480#issuecomment-4757914152","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120480","id":4757914152,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG5gCKA","user":{"login":"PitchBlanc","id":200520065,"node_id":"U_kgDOC_OxgQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200520065?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc","html_url":"https://github.com/PitchBlanc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-20T12:48:37Z","updated_at":"2026-06-20T12:48:37Z","body":"forgot to include that changing switch_mode to immediate stops the errors, but obviously breaks the animations I need to be synced","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4757914152/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4759230312","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120480#issuecomment-4759230312","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120480","id":4759230312,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG6wXaA","user":{"login":"BrastenXBL","id":121268723,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzpp8w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121268723?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrastenXBL","html_url":"https://github.com/BrastenXBL","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrastenXBL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrastenXBL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrastenXBL/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrastenXBL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrastenXBL/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrastenXBL/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrastenXBL/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrastenXBL/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrastenXBL/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-20T17:13:48Z","updated_at":"2026-06-20T17:13:48Z","body":"https://www.reddit.com/r/godot/s/ZpapD8ytiR to repeat\n\nThere are a few complicating factors.\n\nIt seems like your StateMachine for the `right` state isn't complete.\n\nYou also have a code flaw\n\n\tfunc is_walking_right() -> bool:\n\t\treturn speed >= 0.0\n\nshould be\n\n\tfunc is_walking_right() -> bool:\n\t\treturn speed > 0.0\n\nWhat's happening in the MRP is the StateMachine is flowing immediately to the `right` from a `stand`. I'm not totally sure why this throws an error. But fixing this in code resolves that specific MRP ZIP.\n\nI can't get the same error if is_walking_left is altered to \n\n\treturn speed <= 0.0\n\nSo there may be something wrong specifically with `right` animation.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4759230312/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4759283871","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120480#issuecomment-4759283871","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120480","id":4759283871,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG6zonw","user":{"login":"PitchBlanc","id":200520065,"node_id":"U_kgDOC_OxgQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200520065?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc","html_url":"https://github.com/PitchBlanc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PitchBlanc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-20T17:27:07Z","updated_at":"2026-06-20T17:27:07Z","body":"Fixing the is_walking_right in the mrp does stop the error, but it doesn't explain the p_frame out of bounds error.\nLooking at the source code for set_frame() makes me think that p_frame should be the same frame as one of the frames in the animation it tries to sync to, but p_frame value seems to depend entirely on the value of the first frame in the animation. If i swap frames around then the error comes with different p_frame values.\n\nIt doesn't help that I can't reproduce this on 4.6 at all, even with a faulty is_walking_right() ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4759283871/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4761622863","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120480#issuecomment-4761622863","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120480","id":4761622863,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG9CZTw","user":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11736217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb","html_url":"https://github.com/CreatedBySeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-21T10:11:42Z","updated_at":"2026-06-21T10:11:42Z","body":"Even if it can be addressed by fixing the logic error, since this is an error that wasn't present on 4.6 I'm going to put it as a regression. At minimum I think we wouldn't expect to surface a C++ error for bad animation handling code.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comme